# `if ((type as TypeReference).node)`: a store by name appends the field, most objects are without it. The look at the slot parts three ways:
# filled: the typed run . EMPTY, and the object's own byte and the guard of the class say that nothing stands above and nothing lies outside the slots: the read is undefined, the branch folds, the side is three looks and a jump . else closed.
# f1 = use, f2 = flagsOf, f3 = levelOf. A field of the birth (`flags`) gets no such side: its slot is never empty.
# `level: Level` lies in four bytes with marks for absent, undefined and null, and its look asks for a number: it fails on all three, so its failing side is no empty slot: null there is read as null.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: [[filled]]: boolean @Boolean = IsSlotFilled {{*}}key="part"
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch [[filled]] -> taken {{*}}, notTaken [[empty]]()
# CHECK: [[empty]]():
# CHECK-NEXT: = HasNoFieldOutsideSlot
# CHECK: = AreMembersUnchanged {{*}}key="part"
# RUN(BIRTH): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# BIRTH-LABEL: code f2:Body
# BIRTH-NOT: = AreMembersUnchanged
# RUN(RAW): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# RAW-LABEL: code f3:Body
# RAW: = IsSlotFilled {{*}}key="level"{{*}}holdsDeclaredType
# RAW-NOT: = AreMembersUnchanged
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: none
# ANSWERS: has 3
# ANSWERS: has 5
# ANSWERS: has 3
# ANSWERS: none
# ANSWERS: has 2
# ANSWERS: has 0
